  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation Spatial planning for urban and rural development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Uzbekistan has prioritised spatial planning to foster economic growth, attract more investments, and address socio-economic inequalities and the urban-rural divide, ensuring equitable benefits from reforms that have attracted the international attention since 2016. These priorities align with the objectives of the Regional Team Europe Initiative on Digital Connectivity and the Regional Team Europe Initiative on Water, Energy, and Climate as well as with the Global Gateway&#xbf;s 360-degree approach, emphasizing connectivity, climate and digitalisation, while also aiming at improving regulatory framework and national capacities. The Overall Objective of the Action (Impact) is to foster an enabling environment for strategic and sustainable spatial planning in Uzbekistan.</narrative>
  </description>
